WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.950
In 2015, offshore fields gave nearly 30
per cent of the world's oil production.

2
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:08.210
Most came from shallow water.

3
00:00:08.260 --> 00:00:10.810
Now projects are moving into deep water.

4
00:00:10.860 --> 00:00:13.090
But the ocean holds more.

5
00:00:13.140 --> 00:00:14.890
Tides rise and fall.

6
00:00:14.940 --> 00:00:16.150
Waves roll in.

7
00:00:16.200 --> 00:00:19.950
And on the deep sea bed lie
lumps of metal-rich rock.

8
00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:22.650
Which of these could
we actually run out of?

9
00:00:22.700 --> 00:00:24.190
Just the oil and gas?

10
00:00:24.240 --> 00:00:27.570
In this mission, you'll
find out how offshore oil,

11
00:00:27.620 --> 00:00:30.610
wave and tidal power are used and managed.

12
00:00:30.660 --> 00:00:35.910
Then you'll dive to the sea bed, and sort
its metals into ferrous and non-ferrous.

13
00:00:35.960 --> 00:00:40.360
Your mission: decide which of the
ocean's resources we could run out of.
